00:05:06.690 --> 00:05:07.523
Lauren Farkas.

00:05:07.523 --> 00:05:10.813
Question: Does cranberry
juice really help treat UTIs?

00:05:10.813 --> 00:05:13.720
The evidence on this is quite weak.

00:05:13.720 --> 00:05:15.010
The reason we recommend it,

00:05:15.010 --> 00:05:16.250
is it's kind of benign

00:05:16.250 --> 00:05:18.307
unless you're diabetic and
you're getting a huge sugar load.

00:05:18.307 --> 00:05:21.510
The theory was, if you
drink cranberry juice,

00:05:21.510 --> 00:05:24.200
you will then acidify your urine somewhat.

00:05:24.200 --> 00:05:26.148
And then by having your
urine be more acidic,

00:05:26.148 --> 00:05:29.102
it would thereby decrease
the bacteria colonies

00:05:29.102 --> 00:05:31.160
in your urinary tract.

00:05:31.160 --> 00:05:32.515
Now, when we looked at research,

00:05:32.515 --> 00:05:34.523
it's kind of been weak to non-existent

00:05:34.523 --> 00:05:36.248
when it comes to cranberry juice.

00:05:36.248 --> 00:05:37.886
I know a lot of patients that still do it

00:05:37.886 --> 00:05:39.742
cause they like 'natural remedies'.

00:05:39.742 --> 00:05:41.040
But at the end of the day,

00:05:41.040 --> 00:05:42.697
if you have a true
urinary tract infection,

00:05:42.697 --> 00:05:43.840
you're symptomatic,

00:05:43.840 --> 00:05:46.850
you don't want it to spread
higher in your urinary tract

00:05:46.850 --> 00:05:48.551
to your kidneys and
develop a pyelonephritis.

00:05:48.551 --> 00:05:50.536
'Cause that's already a
serious, serious condition.

00:05:50.536 --> 00:05:52.390
'Cause complicated pyelonephritis

00:05:52.390 --> 00:05:54.580
could warrant IV antibiotics.

00:05:54.580 --> 00:05:55.640
Tristin drumm.

00:05:55.640 --> 00:05:57.680
I burnt my hand really bad last night

00:05:57.680 --> 00:05:58.619
but today it's not hurting

00:05:58.619 --> 00:06:01.131
but I also lost the sense
of touch in my fingertips.

00:06:01.131 --> 00:06:02.180
Is this normal?

00:06:02.180 --> 00:06:04.019
Is it normal when you
have damaged your hand

00:06:04.019 --> 00:06:06.610
that you experience possible
neurologic symptoms.

00:06:06.610 --> 00:06:08.134
Yes. Is it ideal? No.

00:06:08.134 --> 00:06:10.550
Should you be evaluated by a doctor? Yes.

00:06:10.550 --> 00:06:11.610
Something else that happens,

00:06:11.610 --> 00:06:12.900
when you have a burn on your hand,

00:06:12.900 --> 00:06:14.136
you can experience contractures,

00:06:14.136 --> 00:06:15.821
which is actually the skin,

00:06:15.821 --> 00:06:19.374
the scar tissue that's being
laid down in lieu of the skin

00:06:19.374 --> 00:06:21.470
can actually contract a little bit

00:06:21.470 --> 00:06:22.989
and your hand might not be as flexible.

00:06:22.989 --> 00:06:24.316
So these are all reasons

00:06:24.316 --> 00:06:25.707
that you should be consulting your doctor

00:06:25.707 --> 00:06:28.630
to make sure you have an
optimal healing process.

00:06:28.630 --> 00:06:30.311
Darryl Hollonquest Jr.

00:06:30.311 --> 00:06:34.060
What's the importance of
sleep for adults over 50?

00:06:34.060 --> 00:06:36.660
Well, the importance of
sleep for those over 50

00:06:36.660 --> 00:06:38.468
is the same that it is under 50.

00:06:38.468 --> 00:06:42.250
Maintenance, repair and
preparation for the next day.

00:06:42.250 --> 00:06:44.048
So get those seven to nine hours of sleep.

00:06:44.048 --> 00:06:46.940
But just remember we've
created a new age category

00:06:46.940 --> 00:06:48.111
for those over the age of 65

00:06:48.111 --> 00:06:50.910
where the sleep requirements
dropped by an hour or two.

00:06:50.910 --> 00:06:51.826
And the reason for that is,

00:06:51.826 --> 00:06:54.740
it's harder to get the
full seven to nine hours.

00:06:54.740 --> 00:06:56.637
It's harder to stay
asleep as you get older.

00:06:56.637 --> 00:06:58.954
The mechanisms in your
brain sort of change.

00:06:58.954 --> 00:07:01.709
Getting a little bit
less once you're 65 plus,

00:07:01.709 --> 00:07:02.960
may be normal for you.

00:07:02.960 --> 00:07:04.681
How do you know when you
should go to a specialist

00:07:04.681 --> 00:07:06.420
rather than your primary care doctor

00:07:06.420 --> 00:07:08.190
or pediatrician or when you should go

00:07:08.190 --> 00:07:10.380
from one specialist to
another for the same reason?

00:07:10.380 --> 00:07:11.438
You should, in my opinion,

00:07:11.438 --> 00:07:14.810
almost always go to see a
primary care doctor first.

00:07:14.810 --> 00:07:15.976
Especially if you have
a good relationship,

00:07:15.976 --> 00:07:18.990
