00:08:10.030 --> 00:08:11.314
Johnmarcus Lopez.

00:08:11.314 --> 00:08:14.160
What can people do to prevent seizures?

00:08:14.160 --> 00:08:16.391
It really depends on what
causes your seizures.

00:08:16.391 --> 00:08:18.935
And a lot of times, especially
for a first time seizure,

00:08:18.935 --> 00:08:21.010
we don't know the answer to that.

00:08:21.010 --> 00:08:23.550
When I worked on the pediatric
ward when I was a resident,

00:08:23.550 --> 00:08:25.730
we would have patients that would come in,

00:08:25.730 --> 00:08:27.270
following a seizure protocol

00:08:27.270 --> 00:08:29.419
where we would actually
try to induce the seizures

00:08:29.419 --> 00:08:31.910
while monitoring their brainwaves

00:08:31.910 --> 00:08:34.412
and things that we used to
do include sleep deprivation,

00:08:34.412 --> 00:08:37.393
intense light therapy
with like flashing lights.

00:08:37.393 --> 00:08:40.400
The question I would pose to you would be,

00:08:40.400 --> 00:08:42.171
A. How do you know it's
definitely a seizure

00:08:42.171 --> 00:08:43.450
that you're experiencing?

00:08:43.450 --> 00:08:45.670
B. Have you seen a
neurologist to figure out

00:08:45.670 --> 00:08:47.610
what type of seizure disorder you have and

00:08:47.610 --> 00:08:49.177
C. Figure out what your triggers are.

00:08:49.177 --> 00:08:51.730
And a lot of times that
means asking you questions

00:08:51.730 --> 00:08:53.250
so you can figure out
what the triggers are.

